Reason: Within the energy sector specifically, decarbonization concentrates job and tax-base losses in fossil-dependent regions. A Nature Communications study records that the decline of the German coal sector since 1960 affected 600,000 jobs, mostly concentrated in the Ruhr region, and warns benefits of the low-carbon electricity build-out tend to flow to already-affluent regions, sustaining inequality



